eb/2","section":6,"section_title":"Exponential smoothing for every partial deck","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:1caa7bdec94c9114641f60fff15a5e059a624a7c452f507aeb58a74fa9a9b4e8","file":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/05-strong-providers.tex","line":344,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"95e7fb8aac75c122f302c0f76ca63a17936fd9f38dd7d0ec3ed530f1164bd146","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/05-strong-providers.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:1caa7bdec94c9114641f60fff15a5e059a624a7c452f507aeb58a74fa9a9b4e8","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/05-strong-providers.tex#L344"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{n:strong-tail}\nThere are absolute constants $a>0$ and $C<\\infty$ such that, for\nevery dyadic $N$, every coordinate order, and every partition\n$\\lambda=(N-k,\\beta)\\vdash N$, with\n$\\beta=(\\lambda_2,\\lambda_3,\\ldots)\\vdash k$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{n:strong-tail-eq}\n \\|T_N(\\lambda)\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}^2\n       \\le e^{Ck}D_\\beta^{-a}.\n\\end{equation}\nHere $D_\\beta=\\dim V_\\beta$, including $D_\\varnothing=1$.\nOne may take $a=1/p'=(p-1)/p$ for the exponent in\nTheorem~\\ref{n:strong-density}."}
